------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THE BULK TIE-RING RELAXATION ON VSS/VDD -- DID IT CAUSE LVS TROUBLE?
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NO. This was the flagged risk (VSS 131.27 -> 28.36 um, 7 -> 4 vias; VDD 131.88 ->
85.07 um, 8 -> 7 vias), so it was checked directly rather than inferred from the
overall verdict:

  - VSS extracts as ONE net and VDD extracts as ONE net.
  - Net count is 10 vs 10. A tie ring SPLIT by a released landing would have shown
    as 11+ layout nets; a ring MERGE/short would have shown as 9 and blocked the
    unique match. Neither occurred.
  - Mechanically this is expected: a tie ring is a single electrical node, so moving
    a landing from one point on the ring to another point on the SAME ring changes
    metal but not connectivity -- invisible to LVS by construction. Confirmed, not assumed.
  - The two extraction shorts the router had predicted (VSS on diff_pair_XMN1_XMN2's
    tap_ring, net8 on XC0's top_met) again did NOT occur; both extracted as distinct nets.

