------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ONE ITEM TO HAND FORWARD (not a mismatch, not a layout fix)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PORT ORDER CHANGED vs pass 1. The extracted netlists differ on exactly ONE line out
of 303 -- the top .subckt declaration:
    pass 1 : .subckt routed vout VDD VSS Vin Vip
    pass 2 : .subckt routed vout Vin Vip VDD VSS
All 247 device lines are byte-identical. The cause is the optimizer relocating the
VDD and VSS met3 (69/20) net labels, which reorders Magic's port emission.

  Impact on LVS : NONE. netgen matches pins by name and reports them equivalent.
  Impact on PEX : REAL, and it belongs to verify-agent, not to the layout. Per
    environment.md's PEX note, a post-layout testbench that instantiates the PEX
    subckt POSITIONALLY must read the port order off the PEX file's own .subckt
    line -- it is neither pass 1's order nor the golden netlist's
    (Vip Vin VDD VSS vout). Flagged so it is not rediscovered as a bogus
    "post-layout gain is wrong" result.
  This is a tooling/ordering note for the orchestrator, NOT a netlist-side fix, and
  emphatically not something to fix by editing the frozen netlist.
